{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Perhaps I shall be built up.</b> From the root of בן. And further, it is possible that the בן is like the form of a building, and the אב is like the foundation. And בן is written deficient heh, and so every term of description, or past-tense verb." "<b>And Abram listened.</b> He said so to her."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:44.601795623Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}